WEBVTT

NOTE Captions for t1-04-abandonment-wound.mp3 — machine-transcribed on-device from the existing audio (SR-472). Not proofread.
NOTE Cues with ids phase-recognise/-regulate/-release/-rise mark where each step begins; js/saferise-poster.js reads them.

00:00:02.190 --> 00:00:04.640
There's a message you haven't had an answer to.

00:00:04.960 --> 00:00:06.710
Or a room that went quiet.

00:00:06.970 --> 00:00:14.810
Or something in how they said good-bye and you've been carrying it around all
day as though it's already been decided.

00:00:14.570 --> 00:00:23.130
Nothing here is going to tell you whether you're being left. That question is
real and it stays open.

00:00:26.050 --> 00:00:31.780
We're working on the state that arrived while you don't know. That's the usual
order.

00:00:32.010 --> 00:00:40.010
The body goes first, the part of you that knows how to handle this comes
second, it's slower, but it's there.

00:00:49.470 --> 00:00:59.890
The next few minutes close some of it.

00:01:00.170 --> 00:01:03.110
Four steps you don't need to keep track

00:01:03.390 --> 00:01:10.550
I'll take you through them.

phase-recognise
00:01:10.960 --> 00:01:15.720
First, we recognise where this is sitting, usually low.

00:01:32.500 --> 00:01:45.180
Sometimes a hum through all of you that won't hold still. Describe it in one
word.

00:01:51.320 --> 00:02:04.860
Adjected now notice something you just described a state and something in your
did the describing

00:02:05.150 --> 00:02:17.010
Those aren't the same. The state is here in the room. You're the one who
noticed it was here.

00:02:16.770 --> 00:02:23.440
You're already standing somewhere slightly outside it and notice what the word
left out.

00:02:23.650 --> 00:02:34.272
It left out them the message, the tone what it probably means, because here's
what's happened. There's a question with no answer yet, and your body has gone

00:02:34.272 --> 00:02:35.770
ahead and answered it.

00:02:36.000 --> 00:02:47.860
That's what it does with silence. It feels it fast, so it is understanding in
an unknown.

00:02:48.340 --> 00:02:50.100
Now go one step deeper

00:02:55.420 --> 00:03:04.340
Underneath it, there's a question with no answer yet, and your body has
already answered it.

00:03:09.350 --> 00:03:22.010
What the silence means about whether you're wanted one layer further down it's
often one of these

00:03:21.770 --> 00:03:27.280
Losing any say in how it goes, being left to deal with it alone.

00:03:27.040 --> 00:03:38.070
Being the problem or running out of time for what you still mean to do if one
landed closer notice which if none did that's fine too

00:03:37.830 --> 00:03:41.760
Either way, leave it where it is. Nothing to solve here.

phase-regulate
00:03:43.930 --> 00:03:57.680
Second, we regulate your physiology to steady the pulse, breathe in for four,
and out for six, longer out than in every time.

00:03:57.440 --> 00:04:07.483
Bring your attention to the middle of your chest. A hand there, if you want
one. Warmth at that spot, does something on its own that nothing you think

00:04:07.483 --> 00:04:08.220
will match.

00:04:07.980 --> 00:04:12.040
You'll feel the pull toward the phone, toward checking.

00:04:12.300 --> 00:04:15.430
Towards saying the thing that would settle it right now.

00:04:15.770 --> 00:04:25.846
It'll still be there in a few minutes. The count first thoughts will come.
Maybe a lot of them. That's what a mind does, and it doesn't mean this isn't

00:04:25.846 --> 00:04:26.380
working.

00:04:26.600 --> 00:04:32.070
When one arrives, let it arrive. Don't push it away. Don't follow away.

00:04:31.830 --> 00:04:43.830
Don't finish it. A thought turning up isn't a thought asking you to act. If
you notice yourself working hard at this, ease off. Watching takes no effort.

00:04:44.060 --> 00:04:46.900
Effort means you've started fighting.

00:04:47.110 --> 00:04:57.110
Whether passes through a room, the room doesn't become the weather. Stay here
in this breathing space, just a moment longer before we move to release.

phase-release
00:05:03.400 --> 00:05:13.340
Third, we release the unnecessary mental labor.

00:05:13.840 --> 00:05:19.550
Look closely at what you are carrying. There's the state and there's the
searching.

00:05:19.310 --> 00:05:30.130
Going back through it, re-reading the message, replaying the conversation,
hunting for the exact moment, the tone changed. Does it ever finish?

00:05:35.960 --> 00:05:44.640
It doesn't.

00:05:46.240 --> 00:05:48.190
Every pause finds something.

00:05:48.400 --> 00:05:58.810
And everything it finds could mean two things, so you go round again. That's
not investigation. That's a circuit. Let the state stay. It's here and

00:05:58.810 --> 00:06:02.280
nobody's arguing with it. Put down the searching.

00:06:02.590 --> 00:06:03.780
Just that.

00:06:04.010 --> 00:06:14.451
We pause here to express deep gratitude to your attention in your heart for
granting you conscious awareness of what has really been driving this trigger

00:06:14.451 --> 00:06:15.270
from within.

00:06:21.840 --> 00:06:29.370
The deep-seated concern that your essential truth needed continuous protection
is intensely real.

00:06:29.610 --> 00:06:36.340
And that hyper-vigilance running silently in the background has been
exhausting your vital force.

00:06:36.620 --> 00:06:41.830
You can thank that vigilant sentinel for standing guard over your worth.

00:06:42.060 --> 00:06:45.220
And gently let it know it can stand down.

00:06:51.740 --> 00:06:52.760
And the question.

00:06:53.170 --> 00:06:56.920
Not what's wrong with me that I'm like this about people.

00:07:02.460 --> 00:07:07.490
You've asked that one a hundred times, and it has never once given you
anything.

00:07:13.710 --> 00:07:14.900
What was this for?

00:07:22.490 --> 00:07:28.000
Something in you moves very fast when connection looks like it might be going.

00:07:34.200 --> 00:07:38.090
Early, hard to argue with, ahead of any sinking.

00:07:43.670 --> 00:07:46.580
That's what protection looks like from the inside.

00:07:46.940 --> 00:07:53.210
Where it learned to do that, that's not today's work, and it isn't mine to
tell you.

00:07:53.450 --> 00:07:55.870
One thing though, before we move.

00:08:01.330 --> 00:08:06.280
If any of that landed, there's usually a second thing right behind it.

00:08:06.550 --> 00:08:10.700
How did I not see this? Look how long I've been doing it.

00:08:11.070 --> 00:08:12.380
Put that down too.

00:08:12.720 --> 00:08:15.750
It's the same thing wearing a different coat.

00:08:21.720 --> 00:08:23.130
You couldn't have seen it.

00:08:29.760 --> 00:08:34.780
It was there before you had a say, and things like that don't announce
themselves.

00:08:35.040 --> 00:08:36.160
You're not late.

00:08:36.390 --> 00:08:40.710
You're here. You don't need the answer now. Keep the question.

00:08:40.950 --> 00:08:43.730
It's worth coming back to when you're steadier.

00:08:43.950 --> 00:08:46.140
Some of this belongs to to-day

00:08:46.380 --> 00:08:56.850
Some of it may be older. You don't have to sort which yet. Just notice there
might be both. Now the one that landed closes if one did.

00:09:04.730 --> 00:09:07.360
Put it where your breath is and leave it there.

00:09:07.710 --> 00:09:10.370
If it was losing any say, you're right.

00:09:17.770 --> 00:09:20.190
Some of this isn't yours to control.

00:09:26.830 --> 00:09:28.630
How you go through it still is

00:09:35.360 --> 00:09:46.830
If it was being left alone, that fear is old, and it has its reasons. You're
not deciding to-day whose days that gets answered later by what happens.

00:09:47.060 --> 00:09:52.830
If it was being the problem, don't test it now, peeking at it from inside the
state.

00:09:53.110 --> 00:09:54.570
Only makes it louder.

00:09:54.890 --> 00:09:56.410
Leave it where it is.

00:09:56.750 --> 00:09:59.320
And notice it didn't come from a good day.

00:10:05.640 --> 00:10:09.030
If it was running out of time, that one's real.

00:10:15.570 --> 00:10:18.250
But nobody can look at something that size.

00:10:18.460 --> 00:10:20.960
While their whole body is braced against it.

00:10:26.790 --> 00:10:28.610
Let go of the bracing.

00:10:28.880 --> 00:10:30.150
Not the fact.

00:10:30.520 --> 00:10:33.750
None of it gets settled from inside this state.

00:10:33.970 --> 00:10:36.710
That's why it waits until you're out of it.

phase-rise
00:10:43.800 --> 00:10:46.170
We rise into centered presence.

00:10:46.430 --> 00:10:51.330
Picture yourself from across the room, phone face down, waiting.

00:10:51.570 --> 00:10:52.880
You don't know yet

00:11:00.310 --> 00:11:03.320
And you're steady enough not to know for a while.

00:11:09.030 --> 00:11:13.650
Now picture the version of you that you'd want to be while you're still
waiting.

00:11:14.040 --> 00:11:17.090
Same silence, same pull to check.

00:11:22.550 --> 00:11:26.100
But you're the one deciding where your attention goes.

00:11:26.450 --> 00:11:27.920
Not on the reply.

00:11:28.230 --> 00:11:30.840
On your own day, where are you?

00:11:31.200 --> 00:11:36.550
What's in your hands? What are you doing that isn't waiting? Now step into it.

00:11:36.800 --> 00:11:43.350
The not knowing is still there. Your attention is where you put it. Pick one
thing you'll do this way.

00:11:43.110 --> 00:11:54.718
Next time the waiting starts, once that moment has happened, look back at it
and write down what was different, one more slow breath, in for four, out for

00:11:54.718 --> 00:11:55.020
six.

00:11:55.260 --> 00:11:56.890
Notice how you are now.

00:12:02.280 --> 00:12:16.040
Different or not, either is fine. Move your hands and feet. Feel the floor
under you. Open your eyes when you're ready.

00:12:22.200 --> 00:12:33.080
Return to this guided meditation as often as you need to until you no longer
do.
